.SH hee-shell(1)
.PP
section: 1 hee-shell -- ssh into a known TCOS host by short alias.
.PP
Real, deliberately thin: this is \f[V]ssh\f[R] with TCOS\[aq]s own host
aliases baked in, not a new protocol or a permissions mechanism.
It cannot grant access a key doesn\[aq]t already have -- if the calling
session\[aq]s key isn\[aq]t authorized on the target host/account, this
fails exactly like a bare \f[V]ssh\f[R] call would, with the same real
error.
.PP
Alias table only includes hosts actually confirmed reachable by name
this session -- not speculative.
Add more here as they\[aq]re verified, not guessed.
.PP
usage: hee-shell <alias|host> [user]
.PP
